    "question_type": "what",
    "interpretation": "Total claim payments with a payment date in May 2026 (1\u201331 May), using the agreed paid_amount metric, which counts payments by payment date. It covers motor and home claims. I excluded the 'reload-2026-05-16' batch because it re-loaded payments that had already arrived in the nightly batches.",
    "answer": "We paid out about $4,485,464 (AUD) on claims in May 2026. The raw warehouse total is $5,214,647. That figure is overstated by $729,183, because a one-off reload on 16 May 2026 loaded 84 payments a second time. I checked that all 84 reloaded rows match a nightly-batch payment on claim, date, amount and payee type.",
    "answer_sql": "SELECT sum(amount) AS paid_may_2026 FROM claim_payments WHERE payment_date BETWEEN '2026-05-01' AND '2026-05-31' AND load_batch NOT LIKE 'reload-%'",
